# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 dayPeriodRuleSet for cy (cldr-json
# cldr-core/supplemental/dayPeriods.json), transcribed in
# chronologia/dayparts.py.  Welsh draws only three bands and has no
# night rule at all, so no night vocabulary ships.
# Unicode CLDR 47, locale cy, gregorian calendar (cldr-json
# cldr-dates-full/main/cy/ca-gregorian.json).
# dayPeriod "morning1"; the stand-alone abbreviated
# name is the single-token surface.  Noun: en.wiktionary.org,
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bore (masculine, plural boreau).  Soft b -> f.
# Soft-mutated surfaces are listed beside the radical: Welsh changes a
# word's first letter after a preceding trigger.  Mutation table:
# en.wikipedia.org, "Welsh mutation".
bore
fore
borau
